To compile the program, use the following command:

```
gcc -o plant_monitor plant_monitor.c -lpigpio -lpthread
```

To run the program, use the following command:

```
./plant_monitor <SPI channel> <ADC channel> <min calibration value> <max calibration value> <moisture threshold> <logging interval>
```

Replace `<SPI channel>`, `<ADC channel>`, `<min calibration value>`, `<max calibration value>`, `<moisture threshold>`, and `<logging interval>` with the appropriate values for your setup.

This program continuously monitors the potted plant's moisture level using a HiLetgo Soil Moisture Sensor connected to the MCP3008 ADC on the SPI bus CE0 (bus 0, channel 0) operating at 500 kHz in single-ended mode. It logs the timestamped moisture percentage to a file named `plant_data.txt` in append mode every 60 seconds in the format "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS, <moisture_percent>". The program accepts command-line arguments to specify the SPI channel, ADC channel, minimum and maximum calibration values, the moisture threshold, the logging interval, the recipient email address, and the path to an msmtp configuration file. It checks every initialization call and each SPI transfer for errors, prints diagnostic messages to stderr, handles a failed ADC read by logging the error to stderr and simply retrying on the next cycle without crashing, and triggers an email alert via msmtp (using pipe to pipe the email body, never shell interpolation) whenever the measured moisture falls below 30 (or the user-specified threshold). The program also validates the msmtp exit status and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM by closing the SPI interface, terminating the driver, freeing any dynamically allocated memory, and exiting cleanly on all exit paths.

