```

To compile the program, save it to a file named `main.c`, and then use the following command:

```
gcc -o main main.c -lgpiod -lpigpio -std=c99
```

This will create an executable file named `main`. To run the program, use:

```
./main
```

The program will continuously monitor the MAX30102 pulse oximeter on I2C bus 1, sampling the SpO₂ and heart-rate values once per second. It will also handle errors and release resources properly.

