This code uses the `gpio_open`, `gpio_direction_output`, `gpio_set_level`, `gpio_close`, `usleep`, and `perror` functions from the Linux GPIO API. It also uses the `fcntl` and `sys_ioctl` functions to open the GPIO device and set the GPIO direction and level.

Please note that this code assumes you have the appropriate permissions to access the GPIO device. If you need to run the program with elevated privileges, you may need to use `sudo` or set the appropriate permissions on the GPIO device.

