Here's the complete, compilable C code that fulfills the user's request using the libgpiod and pigpio libraries. This code continuously reads temperature and humidity from a Sensirion SHT35-DIS-B sensor on I2C bus 1, with clock stretching disabled, waiting at least 15 ms after issuing the command before reading the six-byte result, sampling every 5 seconds. It logs each reading to a CSV file named "environment.csv" with an ISO-8601 timestamp followed by temperature in Celsius and relative humidity in percent, and includes a header row if the file does not already exist or is empty. It also checks the driver initialization, I2C bus opening, every I2C read/write operation, CRC validation, and file opening, printing a descriptive error to stderr on any failure and either continuing or exiting as appropriate.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/ioctl.h>
#include <sys/types.h>
