Here's a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W that reads two Analog Devices ADPD105 photometric front-end sensors on the I2C bus, computes the correlated color temperature (CCT) from the sensor data, and logs the average CCT once per second to a file named `cct_log.csv`. The implementation uses the sensor's API calls or equivalent block reads for register access, verifies the success of every I2C read and write operation, and gracefully logs an error to stderr and skips that cycle's entry on any sensor-absent or bus-error condition. It also ensures that all I2C handles, file streams, and any driver resources are cleanly released on every exit path, including handling of SIGINT and SIGTERM signals.

