This program fulfills the user's request by continuously monitoring the SainSmart IR Flame Sensor Module connected via GPIO, reading the digital output every 50 ms, applying a 50 ms software debounce, and starting a hardware PWM signal at 100 Hz on GPIO18 when a flame is detected. It logs each event to a file named `flame_log.txt` with ISO-8601 timestamps for system start, flame detection, flame end, and program shutdown. The program also verifies successful initialization of the driver library, checks the result of every GPIO read, detects a sensor-absent condition by timing out if no valid reading is obtained, and on receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, it cleanly stops the PWM, resets the GPIO pins, terminates the driver library, and closes the log file.

