This program will continuously read the ambient light from the VEML7700 sensor, apply gamma-corrected scaling to determine the brightness level for the WS2812B LED strip, and drive the strip by bit-banging the data line on GPIO18 (BCM). It will run in an infinite loop with a 200 ms pause between iterations, print the current lux reading and the computed brightness value to stdout each cycle, retry any I2C communication errors up to three times with a 100 ms delay between attempts, log an error and continue if all retries fail, and install signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that gracefully release the GPIO line, close the I2C file descriptor, and turn off the LED strip before exiting.

