Here's a complete, compilable C program for a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B that uses the MPR121 capacitive touch controller on I2C bus 1 to read touch status every 10 ms, debounces touch events with a 100 ms delay, and toggles a 5 V relay connected to GPIO17 (BCM) each time electrode 0 is touched. The program also checks every initialization step and every I2C operation for errors, logs all I2C, GPIO, and configuration errors with timestamps to a file named `touch_relay.log`, and on any failure logs the error and exits gracefully while handling SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to cleanly close the I2C interface, release the GPIO pin, and close the log file.

