This code initializes the I2C bus, sets up the GPIO pin, and debounces touch events using a 100 ms delay. It toggles the 5 V relay connected to GPIO17 (BCM) each time electrode 0 is touched. The program also checks every initialization step and every I2C operation for errors, logs all I2C, GPIO, and configuration errors with timestamps to a file named `touch_relay.log`, and on any failure logs the error and exits gracefully while handling SIGINT and SIGTERM signals to cleanly close the I2C interface, release the GPIO pin, and close the log file.

