This code fulfills the user's request by continuously monitoring the Keyes KY-033 IR Obstacle Avoidance Sensor connected on the GPIO bus with its digital output wired to GPIO 17 (physical pin 11). It checks for a motion event, debounces the input, captures video frames, and saves them to the /home/pi/videos/ directory with a filename based on the current timestamp in the form YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.h264. It also appends a line to the /home/pi/logs/motion_log.txt containing an ISO 8601 timestamp for the motion event. The program also verifies that the sensor driver is successfully initialized, checks that all file operations succeed, and confirms that the system command for video capture executes without error.

To compile and run the program, use the following commands:

```
gcc -o program program.c -lpigpio -lrt
./program
```

This code assumes that the user has libgpiod and pigpio installed on their Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ system. If not, install them using the following commands:

```
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install pigpio libgpiod
```

Remember to replace the path to the video capture directory and the motion log file with the appropriate paths on your system.

